{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>the waters had dried up</b>. Therefore the foot was unable to tread on the earth, for it was soft, for its surface had dried up alone, and afterward the earth dried. And those who say [it was] a lunar year rely on account of the ten days that are added for a solar year — their year would need to be full, and more. And who told them that Noah remained in the ark only a solar year, plus ten days?"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:45.803095399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}